	<p>
		Hello! I'm <strong>Filipe Carmona</strong>, a Senior Software Engineer and Technical Lead with over a decade of experience designing, architecting, and scaling enterprise web applications, distributed cloud services, and applied AI systems. I am based in Santos, São Paulo, Brazil, and work remotely with international teams across North America and globally.
	</p>

	<h2>My Background & Journey</h2>
	<p>
		My engineering career spans 10+ years across fast-growing SaaS startups, enterprise telecommunications, e-commerce marketplaces, and public sector software. Throughout this journey, I have specialized in building accessible, high-performance web applications using <strong>TypeScript</strong>, <strong>React</strong>, <strong>Angular</strong>, and <strong>Node.js</strong>, while managing multi-cloud deployments on <strong>AWS</strong>, <strong>Azure</strong>, and <strong>Google Cloud Platform</strong>.
	</p>

	<h2>Key Career Highlights</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Avaya (2024 – 2025):</strong> As Software Engineer III, I engineered reusable contact center UI widgets deployed across 10+ global enterprise clients, serving 30,000+ daily active agents. I integrated Google Dialogflow for conversational AI, context-aware reply suggestions, and real-time sentiment scoring. Additionally, I authored an internal CLI scaffolding tool published to a private Sonatype Nexus registry, cutting widget setup time by ~70%, and co-managed zero-downtime blue/green Kubernetes releases on AWS.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Sowingo (2016 – 2023):</strong> Over 7+ years, I evolved from Frontend Developer to Senior Developer and Team Lead. I architected the phased, zero-downtime migration of a 50-screen enterprise healthcare web app from AngularJS to React 17/TypeScript via Web Components. I mentored junior software engineers, implemented electronic patient health records strictly adhering to the HL7 FHIR standard with HIPAA compliance, built low-latency real-time clinical messaging, and helped scale the platform to support over 8,000 dental clinics across North America.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Entrepreneurship & Early Career:</strong> Co-founded B2B e-procurement marketplace CotaBox, engineered lightweight IoT and digital signage web interfaces at Mobbit IoT Enabler, and developed municipal administrative systems in Java EE and PHP for Prodesan.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Applied AI & Lifelong Learning</h2>
	<p>
		Technology evolves rapidly, and I am committed to continuous growth. I am currently pursuing a <strong>Graduate Certificate in Software Engineering with Applied AI</strong> at UNIPDS (2026–2027), focusing on enterprise distributed architectures, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), conversational agent assist, and local LLM orchestration (Ollama, LM Studio). I hold a Technologist Degree in <strong>Systems Analysis and Development</strong> from FATEC Santos (2010–2014).
	</p>

